// REJECTED — a method-local `let` may not shadow an activation-body binding.
//
// The activation body already refuses a duplicate binding ("name `store` is
// already bound in C"); a provide-method body consulted only its own params
// and locals, so the collision passed. It is not a scoping nicety: a method
// body lowers into a closure over the activation frame and the safe-name
// allocator drew from the method's names alone, so the shadowing binding was
// emitted with the SAME host-safe name as the component local. The component
// local's declared inverse then ran against the shadow — `store.drop()` on a
// `Str` — and the host Map it was supposed to release leaked. With the
// shadowing `let` written AFTER the use, as here, the local is not bound at
// all and teardown raises.
//
// expected error:
//   `store` is already bound in `set`

service Cache { fn set(key: Str) }

component C provides cache: Cache {
  let store = effect Map.new() undo store.drop()
  provide cache {
    fn set(key) {
      effect store.insert(key, "v")
      undo   store.remove(key)
      let store = key
    }
  }
}
